## Details

### WP-35 Adaptive QA and critical reinspection (scope split from WP-16)
- General profile structures and host integration for producer-specific QA intensity;
  CP owns the sample and trusted producer history. Client consumes assigned units,
  never chooses them. Maintainer values: novice up to100%, standard10%, three clean
  cells ->5%, three more -> sparse inspection, error in sparse phase ->10%.
  D-46: sparse mode checks every third cell (skips two);10%/5% refers to each
  inspected cell's area. Preserve producer-specific policy/history in CP/DP.
- Critical severity blocks and requires an explicit search for similar errors
  across the assigned reinspection territory. Non-critical needs a local fix.
  Preserve the obligation after the original defect is fixed until its evidence
  is satisfied; do not equate fix-approved with territory reinspection completed.
  D-46 limits the similar-error search to the current cell. Persist assignment and
  release evidence in CP/DP; consume WP-16's explicit pending-reinspection boundary.
  Migrate WP-15's class-only blocking API schema-first, preserving old tests/v1 taxonomy.
- Accept: deterministic state-transition/streak/reset tests, no client sample
  selection, severity-driven blocker tests, and critical reinspection persisting
  beyond local fix. CP/DP policy execution is an external integration dependency.

### WP-00 Repository bootstrap
- npm workspaces root; the six packages and `plans/` as empty workspaces with `index.js` and `README.md` (module cards in
  `planned` state); `.npmrc` with the `@geoiplus` scope on CodeArtifact (`brandbook:README.md`), token from the environment.
- Tooling: ESLint (errors only), Vitest, `tsc --checkJs --noEmit` over JSDoc, `check:arch` = dependency-cruiser rules from
  STRUCTURE.md §3 + the 300-line maintenance advisory (D-20) + protection rules (P2 chunk isolation, no P4) + CSS token rule (UI spec §9),
  `size-limit`, API report generation, changesets, `npm run index` (port `geoviewer:scripts/project-index.mjs`).
- CI workflow running `npm run check`; PR template from AGENTS.md §10.
- Accept: `npm ci && npm run check` passes on the empty skeleton; a planted forbidden import, a cycle and a
  literal colour in a component CSS each make `check:arch` fail (tests for the checker). A 301-line source file produces
  a maintenance advisory, not a failure (maintainer clarification D-20).

### WP-01 Contract schemas
- Port `seameditor:contracts/schemas/{common,seam.reroute,seam.assign,seam.vertex_move,seam.vertex_insert,edit-instruction}`
  unchanged (record the revision). New drafts: `dtm.interpolate_boundary`, `dtm.plane_fit`, `dtm.remove_spikes`
  (parameters with `TBD` ranges and proposed defaults), `dtm-patch`, `defect`, `scan-evidence`, `result-manifest`.
- Accept: every schema compiles with Ajv 2020; valid and invalid examples per schema.

### WP-02 Plans and fixtures
- `contracts/plan.schema.json` from workspace-plans-spec.md §2; `contracts/extension-orthoqm.schema.json` draft from the
  field table of the library spec §3; `plans/orthoqm/{production,qa-sampling}.plan.json`; golden fixtures of
  workspace-plans-spec.md §8 (contracts only; expected outputs filled by WP-21).
- Accept: both plans validate; every fixture contract validates against the Operaflow schema at the pinned revision or is an
  intended-invalid case.

### WP-03 ... WP-22
Acceptance criteria are the "Accept:" lines of the module's section in [orthoqm-library-spec.md §6](specs/orthoqm-library-spec.md#6-modules).
Specific notes:
- **WP-07** writes a generator script (`fixtures/generate/`) using GDAL from a pinned container image or the local GDAL, and
  commits the outputs (total <= 5 MB). Cameras, DTM and frames are consistent: rectifying the frames with the DTM gives the
  per-image orthos (the oracle for WP-17).
- **WP-13** keeps the donor API unchanged; split files over 300 lines only where the property tests stay green; record
  bench results of the plain build in the module card (WP-30 adds the protected comparison).
- **WP-14** may use pinned local `platform-grid-scan` and `gridScanStorage.js` under D-29; record full SHA, paths and hashes without modifying/publishing the donor.
- **WP-21** consumes D-25 schema errors as blocked readiness: show the offending field/path and report the issue to CP. Core WP-03 returns explicit diagnostics; it does not send notifications itself.
- **WP-17** starts as early as its dependencies allow: it is the main technical risk. Without passing its gate the DTM editor
  stays disabled in every plan.
- **WP-22** mock serves: session exchange, contract, plan + signed chunk URLs, manifest and assets, edits (accept / conflict /
  reject), progress, issues, results, and fault injection (stale lease, revoke, offline, duplicate).
  D-47/D-48: cover the authoritative final-output/review lifecycle and refuse completion/release when required final
  areas are unchecked or the reviewed final version is stale. Agree the origin asset adapter (Q-38) before exchange code.

### WP-23 ... WP-31
Acceptance criteria are in [ui-components-spec.md](specs/ui-components-spec.md) (catalogue rows and §9) and in the module
sections of the library spec. [WP-28](work-packages/WP-28.md) now owns both former WP-28/29 journeys (library spec §2.1/§2.2),
bootstrap, schema/graph validation, lifecycle/host tests and mock E2E in both themes; WP-29 is superseded, not completed.
- **WP-25, D-42:** bookmark-style jump from a defect to its location; quick accept/reject;
  rejection requires a nonblank text reason (free comment or standard description).
  Show the append-only verification history and rejection rationale for operator rework.
  D-43: QA also sees authorized prior-version corrections, findings and returns,
  even when the reviewer changes; past records are read-only and keep their versions.
- **WP-27, D-47/D-48:** fast preliminary rectification preview, then queued background final output; cancel/discard stale
  work, distinguish preview/final versions. Generate mandatory final-output bookmarks for changed areas with navigation,
  explicit checking and remaining count. New final versions invalidate affected confirmations. Design schemas/persistence
  first; this is a recorded follow-up to completed WP-17, not an added CPU-kernel implementation in that WP.
- **WP-28, D-48:** end-to-end completion/release is blocked until final jobs succeed and every required changed area is
  checked on the actual current final imagery. Preview approval, mere bookmark visitation and computation completion
  cannot satisfy the gate. Test rejection/re-edit/recompute, stale result arrival and session recovery. Operator may
  continue other editing while background jobs run (D-47); origin release/mosaic processing follows final review (Q-38).

### WP-33 Agent skills
- Drafted: the 12 recovered skills in .claude/skills, written from the specs and templates (no new rules).
- Remaining: each skill passes its WP-34 eval task twice; adjust the description or steps where an agent did not load or
  follow it; prune a skill no task uses.

### WP-34 Agent evals
- `docs/agent-evals/<task>/` with the task prompt, the starting state (a branch or fixture), the rubric graded on the final
  result; tasks per AGENTS.md §12; a runner that records the outcome and timestamps of each run.
- Accept: every task runs twice on the current instructions and the baseline scores are recorded in DECISIONS.md.

### WP-32 Measurements
- Measure the gates of the library spec §8 on the pilot hardware profile; write the numbers into the plan budgets and the
  CI gates; record them in DECISIONS.md.

### WP-36 UI Storybook and synchronised component documentation
- Maintainer request (2026-10-30): after WP-23, create actual Storybook for the UI library,
  showing every component, accepted parameters, properties/methods and useful states.
- Use current official Storybook practices and pinned compatible dependencies. Keep
  the core framework-free; no React wrapper/domain UI implementation is included.
- Story controls, API/arg tables, usage/lifecycle docs, themes/locales and interactive
  examples must reflect actual public exports/JSDoc, with synthetic fixtures only.
- Automate metadata/docs generation or validation and add CI coverage/staleness gates;
  a public UI change cannot silently leave Storybook stale or omit a component.
- Add concise agent instructions plus the recurring procedure in a linked skill:
  every UI API/behaviour change updates its stories/docs/tests in the same change.
  This instruction addition is explicitly requested by the maintainer; do not delay
  it for the not-yet-implemented WP-34 eval suite or silently weaken existing rules.
- Accept: all current component factories and icons documented, meaningful controls
  and API properties visible, lifecycle cleanup verified, a11y/interaction checks,
  both themes, static Storybook build and automatic sync gate pass, plus full check.
- Start in a fresh session/managed checkout from the commit carrying
  [.agent/handoff-WP-36.md](../.agent/handoff-WP-36.md). Local commits only.

### WP-40 ... WP-55 UI system plan (owner-approved 2026-11-07)
Source: [Geoinnovation+ UI system: plan for the first steps](https://claude.ai/artifact/Ujk5d2JiWszeo8fLtcnyHm) (step 3
work packages, step 5 agent kit, start briefs). WP-38 and WP-39 stay reserved for the WP-37 review follow-ups.
- **WP-54** is step 1a: `main` is cut from `c37c2cf`, the last commit before WP-28, plus the Linux `storybook:check` fix.
  WP-28 stays on its branch and merges `main` forward when it resumes. It still owes `MeasurePanel`'s 4 baselines.
- **WP-55** is the first part of step 4 (written guidance only); the templates follow once step 3 has components.
- Rules from the plan: one WP per branch and PR; an ADR for any public API or dependency change; behaviour stays
  (callbacks, data contracts, keyboard paths); every component starts `experimental` and becomes `reviewed` after fixes
  and owner approval. Sizes marked TBD were not given per WP in the plan.
- Step 1b (publish `@geoiplus/ui`, depends on WP-40) has no WP number yet.
